{% import "_shared.html.j2" as sh %}
<div class="lgd-pilot lgd-agg-page" style="{{ sh.container }}">
{# NO h1 in the body: the Flex default page template injects page.title as the served H1 (verified live 2026-08-09); page.title carries the scheme H1, the long SEO title lives in global.title_tag. #}
{{ sh.header(h1, index_url, brand_line, cycle_label, data_date_h) }}

<p style="{{ sh.body_p }}"><strong>What this page is.</strong> There is no public transaction record of lab grown diamond resales, and this page does not claim one. What can be measured honestly is <em>listing-price history</em>: how retailers have repriced the same certified stones over time, and how quickly stones leave the market. That history is the best public context for what a lab grown diamond might be worth later.</p>

<h2 style="{{ sh.h2s }}">Same-stone repricing, April to {{ cycle_label }}</h2>
<p style="{{ sh.body_p }}">Tracking identical certified stones (same certificate number, same retailer) listed in both April and July 2026. Attribution basis: this comparison covers the {{ rep.panel | length }} tracked US retailers whose public listings carry third-party certificate numbers ({{ rep.panel | join(", ") }}); retailers without published certificate numbers cannot be stone-matched and are not part of this statistic.</p>
<div style="{{ sh.callout }}">
<ul style="margin:0;padding:0 0 0 18px;color:#ffffff;line-height:1.65;">
  <li><strong>{{ "{:,}".format(rep.n_pairs) }}</strong> matched listings were live in both months.</li>
  <li>Median listed-price change: <strong>{{ "%+.1f" | format(rep.median_change_pct) }}%</strong> over the three months.</li>
  <li><strong>{{ "%.0f" | format(rep.share_down_pct) }}%</strong> of matched listings were repriced downward.</li>
  <li>Of the {{ "{:,}".format(rep.n_april_stones) }} certified stones tracked in April, <strong>{{ "%.0f" | format(rep.delisted_share_pct) }}%</strong> no longer appeared in the July listings of the {{ rep.panel | length }} certificate-carrying retailers above (sold, delisted, or moved to a retailer outside this panel; public data cannot distinguish which).</li>
</ul>
</div>
<p style="{{ sh.body_p }}">Because these are the same physical stones at the same retailers, this comparison is free of the inventory-mix distortion that affects month-to-month median charts.</p>

<h2 style="{{ sh.h2s }}">Pooled listing-price history (1 carat round)</h2>
<div style="{{ sh.wrap }}">
<table class="lgd-history-table" style="{{ sh.table }}">
  <thead><tr><th style="{{ sh.th_l }}">Month</th><th style="{{ sh.th_r }}">Pooled median</th><th style="{{ sh.th_r }}">Listings (n)</th><th style="{{ sh.th_r }}">Retailers</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for hrow in hist %}
    {% if hrow.n >= 30 %}
    {% set bg = loop.cycle("#fafafa", "#ffffff") %}
    <tr><td style="{{ sh.td(bg) }}font-weight:700;white-space:nowrap;">{{ hrow.label }}</td><td style="{{ sh.tdn(bg) }}">{{ hrow.median | usd }}</td><td style="{{ sh.tdn(bg) }}">{{ "{:,}".format(hrow.n) }}</td><td style="{{ sh.tdn(bg) }}">{{ hrow.retailers }}</td></tr>
    {% endif %}
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p style="{{ sh.note }}">Each month pools only retailers with at least 30 qualifying listings that month.</p>
{% for hrow in hist %}{% if hrow.n >= 30 and hrow.partial_note %}<p style="{{ sh.note }}"><strong>Coverage note.</strong> {{ hrow.partial_note }}</p>{% endif %}{% endfor %}
<p style="{{ sh.note }}"><strong>Composition caveat.</strong> Pooled medians move with inventory mix as well as price; the same-stone repricing figures above are the cleaner signal.</p>

<h2 style="{{ sh.h2s }}">What this means for resale value</h2>
<p style="{{ sh.body_p }}">Falling new-stone listing prices compress what any reseller can expect: a buyer can compare a resale offer against a brand-new certified equivalent in seconds. The honest summary of the data above: new-listing prices for the same stones have been drifting down, and any resale estimate should be anchored to current new-listing prices, not the original purchase price. This page presents listing-price history and delisting behavior only; it does not report resale transactions and makes no promise about resale proceeds.</p>

{{ sh.stat_distinction() }}
{{ sh.loose_stone_note() }}
{{ sh.delist_note(data_date_h, retailer_names) }}
{{ sh.methodology(data_date_h) }}
{{ sh.related(related) }}
{{ sh.footer() }}

<script type="application/ld+json">{{ json_ld | tojson }}</script>
</div>
